WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.187
Visualization should respect the variable structure.

00:00:03.187 --> 00:00:06.597
Bar charts work well for nominal categories.

00:00:06.597 --> 00:00:10.297
Ordered bars preserve the order of ordinal categories.

00:00:10.297 --> 00:00:14.422
Histograms show the distribution of continuous numeric variables.

00:00:14.422 --> 00:00:18.702
Scatterplots show relationships between two numeric variables.

00:00:18.702 --> 00:00:26.742
A chart should make the intended comparison easier without adding structure that the data does not contain.

00:00:26.742 --> 00:00:32.022
For example, connecting unordered categories with a line can accidentally imply continuity.

00:00:32.022 --> 00:00:37.967
Connect this idea to an e-commerce team preparing customer, purchase, and web-event data.

00:00:37.967 --> 00:00:43.587
Ask what could go wrong if the concept were misunderstood: could rows be duplicated,

00:00:43.587 --> 00:00:51.197
important records disappear, categories be interpreted incorrectly, or a report become difficult to reproduce?

00:00:51.197 --> 00:00:57.107
A strong analyst can explain both the SQL operation and the assumption behind it.

00:00:57.107 --> 00:01:03.040
After the example, summarize the idea in one plain-language sentence before moving on.
